WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:10.340
- [Crystal] I feel like I was dehydrated.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.173
Okay.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.551
- [Interviewer] Crystal?
- [Crystal] Yes?

00:00:13.551 --> 00:00:14.820
- [Interviewer] Crystal,
where are you from originally,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.080
where'd you grew up?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.450
- I grew up in two different places

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.660
like Violet Hill, Arkansas

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.940
and I grew up in Beaverton, Michigan.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.680
- [Interviewer] Okay, and
how was your childhood?

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.302
Did you grow up with both your parents?

00:00:27.302 --> 00:00:28.200
- No,

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.610
my father was...

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.840
I found him when I was three,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.230
hanging from our basement rafters

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.600
but my mom and I had a stepdad who was

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.920
60 years older than me;

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.790
he was in World War II, so...

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:44.530
- [Interviewer] So your dad hung himself?

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.390
- Yeah, he had mental issues

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.470
and they put him in a psych ward,

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.990
and then a week later he was...

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.650
He wasn't supposed to get out
and the doctors let him out

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.220
and he took a whole bottle
of Librium, I think it was,

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.323
and he hung himself.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.480
Yeah, and the suicide note
was a week before that,

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.350
you know, I don't know.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.560
I don't really remember much.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.460
I do remember pushing his
dead body a little bit,

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.453
so I have PTSD from that, but...

00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:09.329
- [Interviewer] How old were you?

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:10.988
- I was about three and a half.

00:01:10.988 --> 00:01:12.672
I'm 36 now.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.759
So I mean, it never
really bothered me though.

00:01:14.759 --> 00:01:15.650
- [Interviewer] How was your childhood

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:17.820
with your stepdad and your mom?

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:18.900
- Honestly, I think I had

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.650
the most beautiful childhood
anybody could ever have.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.010
I was very fortunate.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:23.843
I grew up

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.740
at least on 80 acres; we ran a horse farm

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.010
and you know I had nothing
but nature and animals.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.440
- [Interviewer] It was
in Arkansas or Michigan?

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.630
- Both.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.683
Arkansas was more prettier.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.160
That was a rural area.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.720
Violet Hill, Arkansas was like

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.043
there was a school, a post office,

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.590
convenience store.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.810
And my driveway was two miles long

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.520
dirt road.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:53.900
It was just, it was so pretty.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.230
And then

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.237
yeah, I miss that place.

00:01:57.237 --> 00:01:58.377
- [Interviewer] And then
where'd your life go

00:01:58.377 --> 00:01:59.210
when you left home?

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.738
What age did you leave home?

00:02:00.738 --> 00:02:03.210
- I left home at 16.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.760
My stepdad had died and
then my mom moved in

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.650
her current husband, which is Tom,

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.510
and we didn't get along.

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.200
He was really not my friend.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.430
And so that was a messy move-out

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.080
so I couldn't be there anymore.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.470
So at 16, I moved out with my kids' dad,

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.240
my first two kids' dad,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.300
and that was quite interesting.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.140
He worked all the time
and I got to stay home.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.793
- [Interviewer] So you have how many kids?

00:02:32.753 --> 00:02:34.610
- All together, I have four kids.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:35.490
- [Interviewer] Did you raise all four?

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.930
- No.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.990
My first two were with me
until my oldest son was six,

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.600
my daughter was three,

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.430
and then Levi...

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.860
He's still was his dad and family.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.323
And then my youngest son,

00:02:49.757 --> 00:02:52.690
he's three and a half now, four...

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.640
He was born two months early

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.920
and he is with the father's daughter,

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.367
which isn't his blood daughter
but pretty much his daughter.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.350
- [Interviewer] And so you're
living here on the street now?

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.183
- Yeah.

00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:07.500
- [Interviewer] You're in a tent?

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.659
- No.

00:03:08.659 --> 00:03:09.610
No.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.390
I live in the racks

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.853
and I live in like kind of a bird's nest.

00:03:13.853 --> 00:03:15.753
I don't really want to live in a tent.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.840
I can't be city-bound
like this really bad.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.860
I go up to like, I think it's...

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:26.230
If you know where chats
chat or what is it?

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.580
I'm not really even from
here, I'm from Michigan

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.170
and me and my boyfriend came
down here but, it's a park.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.500
- [Interviewer] How long
you been in Skid Row?

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.723
- A month, month and a half.

00:03:34.723 --> 00:03:35.600
- [Interviewer] Oh, that's it?

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:36.610
- Yeah.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.750
It's different.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.039
- [Interviewer] What's your drug?

00:03:39.039 --> 00:03:39.872
- I like...

00:03:39.872 --> 00:03:41.530
I prefer black, as they call it;

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.940
heroin but...

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.850
I mean, I do both but
I don't like that ice.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.490
It makes me real sick.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:48.680
- [Interviewer] You do
both heroin and what else?

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.513
- Ice.

00:03:49.513 --> 00:03:50.436
And I smoke weed.

00:03:50.436 --> 00:03:51.269
- [Interviewer] Ice is...

00:03:51.269 --> 00:03:52.830
Cocaine?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.880
- They call it clear.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:55.830
Meth.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:56.760
- [Interviewer] Crystal meth?

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:57.593
- Yeah.

00:03:57.593 --> 00:03:58.426
- [Interviewer] Got it.

00:03:58.426 --> 00:03:59.923
And what do you do for money?

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.684
What a lot of girls do?

00:04:03.684 --> 00:04:04.870
- No.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.080
I dumpster-dive.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:09.330
Like the other day I pulled
a canopy out of a dumpster

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.400
and I got like 150 for that.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.430
I found a convertible thing.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:14.883
That was 150.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.120
Or, you know,

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.090
you go over to Walgreens
and you stand there

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.491
and people will just hand you money

00:04:21.491 --> 00:04:24.400
or items I'll just trade, you know...

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.290
or I'll call my mom.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.120
That's once a month, so...

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.070
Can I put this out somewhere?

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.011
- [Interviewer] Yeah, you can
just put it out on the floor.

00:04:34.011 --> 00:04:35.011
- Thank you.

00:04:36.837 --> 00:04:38.895
- [Interviewer] Did you
ever talk to your kids?

00:04:38.895 --> 00:04:40.340
- Not really.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.010
My first two kids...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.860
My mom and their dad...

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:46.977
That's a really rough situation.

00:04:46.977 --> 00:04:50.160
My first two kids' dad, I
was with him for 11 years.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.240
So I was 16 til I was 27

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.770
and those two kids were my life, like...

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.050
Nobody helped me, the dad wasn't there

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.640
and me and my son

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.500
we bonded really good,

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.800
but my mom kind of took my kids over

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.400
when I lost my apartment

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.650
because I was cooking meth really bad

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.630
and she was like sending me out the door,

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:14.463
you know what I mean?

00:05:14.463 --> 00:05:16.390
So it's been about 10 years

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.330
since I seen my first two kids

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.200
and then Eli

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:24.020
he was in Kalamazoo and I
was running around Kalamazoo.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.640
And the little one I never see.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.290
I adopted him out.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:28.650
It's just hard for me to see him.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.053
His dad was just murdered
while I was in jail.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.300
Bludgeoned to death by a baseball bat.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.740
So yeah,

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:37.817
that was rough.

00:05:37.817 --> 00:05:40.481
- [Interviewer] So you
were in jail for what?

00:05:40.481 --> 00:05:42.610
- I was in jail this last time...

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.260
I took drug court,

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:45.630
which in Michigan...

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.900
In Michigan, meth is a felony

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:53.750
and I had possession of meth pop up

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:56.500
and then I took awhile, that one.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.903
And before that I had
got a possession of meth

00:05:59.903 --> 00:06:04.903
and a (muffled) charge so I
was facing all three of those

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.400
and a marijuana charge.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:10.320
So I took drug court, which
is like an 18-month program.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.110
And well, I knew that wasn't going to work

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.740
so I went through the loops with that,

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:18.630
got caught and then they
took me off drug court

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.943
and gave me nine months.

00:06:21.039 --> 00:06:21.890
- [Interviewer] Do you ever have contact

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:23.253
with your mom and stepdad?

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.540
- My stepdad died when I was like,

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.710
before I moved out or,

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:33.835
it was after we moved to Mount
Pleasant, but he died 97.

00:06:33.835 --> 00:06:35.450
And then my mom,

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.070
we talk but me and my mom aren't close.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:40.140
I mean, she was sleeping
with my first kids' dad

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:41.550
and I didn't find that out til later

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.690
but she's just been really kind of rotten

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.673
and she doesn't even let me see my kid.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:50.070
She has Bella and then
Caleb is with his dad

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.383
but those two are...

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.630
It's hard for me to talk to her

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.280
when she would bring my kids down

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.790
and go to the Christmas party
at my aunt's house, you know,

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:01.623
five miles away

00:07:01.623 --> 00:07:04.160
and she couldn't even bring
them over to see me, you know?

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.200
So I don't think my daughter
even knows who I am really.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.140
I mean, she knows who I am, but
we don't really talk at all.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.110
It's hard.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.270
My mom's just, she hurts me a lot.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.840
- [Interviewer] And your
boyfriend now is a good guy?

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:17.860
- He's a good guy.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:20.400
I guess we're going
through some tough times.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.000
I have been with him since June.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.400
What about him is we
have the same birthday.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.650
It's weird.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.403
I'm a few hours earlier.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.530
He is a good guy, but he's kinda...

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:34.670
He's from Kalamazoo

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:37.110
and people from Kalamazoo
don't usually come out.

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.390
The only reason I'm here is 'cause of him.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.263
I never wanted to come to California.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.693
He wanted to get high under a bridge.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.300
The lead singer of Red Hot
Chili Peppers or something

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.520
sings Under the Bridge

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.480
and he wants to go under a
bridge and OD or something.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:53.490
I don't know.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.020
And also he was facing
some felony charges.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.623
So, you know...

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:01.130
He just got done doing
five years in prison.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.670
So I got my friend to drive
us out here and drop us off

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.140
but he was supposed to be
working and stuff, you know

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.700
and that guy didn't come through.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:11.718
So we got stuck in the street.

00:08:11.718 --> 00:08:12.551
- [Interviewer] So where do you suppose

00:08:12.551 --> 00:08:14.043
your life will go from here?

00:08:14.043 --> 00:08:15.580
- I don't know.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:18.473
Honestly, right now I
think about death a lot.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:21.680
It seems like it would
just be a lot easier

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.630
'cause I just get tired of it.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.640
I've been in the street a good six years.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:28.600
And when I say in the streets,

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.540
I don't just go sleep in people's houses.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.550
I'm not your average girl.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.750
I don't mingle with men.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:36.180
You know what I mean?

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.230
I usually just stay to my partner, but...

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.900
if there's any help me
and my boyfriend Blake

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.420
would like to get clean together.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.840
I feel like that's the
only way that I'm (muffled)

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.560
is if somebody is doing it with me.

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.090
It's hard for me because

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.280
I mean, I've always been on...

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:57.440
I started shooting up drugs
when I was nine, or no 12,

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.900
but I started smoking weed
and stuff when I was nine

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:03.290
but I did start shooting up cocaine at 12.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.310
So I've been a drug addict
for quite a long time.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.590
- [Interviewer] You told me
your childhood was perfect.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:09.050
- Yeah, that was pretty.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.233
Yeah, but I was curious.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.400
At 12, my mom...

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.060
The internet was out

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:19.020
and my mom never really watched me.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:21.420
My childhood wasn't perfect,
but it was very nice.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:25.050
I mean, I always had room
to run and animals play with

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.270
but I never had any friends.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:27.780
I was very, very isolated

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.870
and I really didn't have no friends.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.703
But at 12,

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:33.330
yeah, I got on the internet.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.550
I was meeting guys off the internet at 12.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:37.666
I really started going downhill at 12

00:09:37.666 --> 00:09:39.720
and my mom didn't really care

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.480
and my stepdad, you know,

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.800
he was there.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.963
So yeah, I started using.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.770
- [Interviewer] Where'd
you get introduced to drugs

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.017
at that young age?

00:09:51.251 --> 00:09:52.150
- Well,

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.250
it wasn't hard.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.500
I always hung out with older people;

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.400
when I was in middle school,

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.950
I was having high schoolers
pick me up to go party.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:02.210
My best friend was in high school

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.713
so I kind of always hung
out with older people.

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:08.140
I guess I never really
fit in with my crew.

00:10:11.007 --> 00:10:13.386
- [Interviewer] And you
left home at an early age?

00:10:13.386 --> 00:10:14.219
- Yeah.
- Is this

00:10:14.219 --> 00:10:15.350
because you didn't get along with stepdad?

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.873
- Yeah, he was really weird, and...

00:10:17.873 --> 00:10:20.490
He kinda moved in and it was uncomfortable

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.323
because my mom was like,

00:10:21.323 --> 00:10:22.410
"Oh, you're just jealous,"

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.980
and maybe I was, I mean...

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.430
My mom was all I had, you know,

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.810
besides my grandma and I don't
know, he just was like...

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:33.572
Took over and was mean
and try to, she's like,

00:10:33.572 --> 00:10:36.130
"You're just jealous because
I spend more time with him,"

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:39.080
and she was drinking and it was just...

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:40.060
I didn't want to be there anymore.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:41.230
He made me feel really weird.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:44.330
And I had a boyfriend
at the time that worked

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:47.170
and we got our own place,

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.040
